{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b5b4b612-8c96-4105-aa40-0800980fbf7e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-954351cbef064fe3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-j2d1wnw7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-E001.md","content":"# Investigation: evaluation execution engine decision\n\n## Description\n\nResolve the strategy's first open question: should the platform build on\nTrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview, already wrapping lm-evaluation-harness) as\nthe single evaluation execution path, or is a new evaluation service needed that\ncan also serve Llama Stack's eval provider API? This is the gating decision for\nthe entire execution layer of the evaluation capability — it determines which\ndownstream implementation epics exist and what they do.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Analyze the LMEvalJob CRD and job runner (trustyai-service-operator, upstream\n  and midstream) against the full set of execution requirements: evaluating\n  models served on KServe endpoints and on Llama Stack distributions, custom\n  evaluation tasks (user-supplied datasets and metrics), and result emission.\n- Analyze Llama Stack's eval provider API surface (meta-llama/llama-stack\n  upstream) and determine what a platform-backed provider must implement, and\n  whether the LMEvalJob path can back it (e.g. via an adapter) or whether the\n  API shape demands a purpose-built service.\n- Assess operational fit: multi-tenancy per data science project, job lifecycle\n  and status reporting, resource/GPU scheduling behavior, and Tech Preview\n  maturity risks of building the P0 path on LMEvalJob.\n- Produce a written recommendation with a decision record covering both\n  outcomes, including repo/component placement if a new service is recommended\n  (new opendatahub-io repo vs. extension of an existing one), and the concrete\n  API/CR surface each downstream epic would build against.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** the LMEvalJob source and the Llama Stack eval provider API\n  specification, **when** the gap analysis is complete, **then** a\n  recommendation document exists that selects exactly one execution approach,\n  with an explicit rationale and a list of gaps each approach must close.\n- **Given** the recommendation, **then** the downstream execution-path plan for\n  the selected outcome is confirmed as buildable (or adjusted), measured by\n  sign-off from the TrustyAI team and the RHOAI GenAI team.\n- The decision record states the API/CR surface downstream consumers\n  (Dashboard, Data Science Pipelines, Llama Stack provider) will build against\n  for the selected outcome.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0, launch evaluation of served model): this investigation decides the\n  architecture of the epic that delivers HLR-1.\n- HLR-7 (P1, Llama Stack eval provider backed by platform service): the\n  provider-API analysis here determines whether HLR-7 is an adapter or native\n  wiring.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42166,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab59d602e88fa4e","agent_id":"ae71d3c6187365b78","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"57e688a8-4d9c-4824-9162-18f13ce1cc8f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:54:48.162Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
