{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-83930076-8a17-4315-b8ef-4d587d86a387","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad3e156a7d0895b9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-j2d1wnw7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-E004.md","content":"# Standard benchmark suites available out of the box\n\n## Description\n\nDeliver the platform's out-of-the-box library of standard benchmark suites\n(e.g. MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag exposed through lm-eval task names) so users can\nselect a standard suite when launching an evaluation, per the licensing\nassessment's packaging determination. This epic packages and ships the suites;\nit does not change the execution engine itself.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Package the standard benchmark suites determined to be redistributable so\n  they are available in disconnected environments without customer action.\n- Provide the customer-fetch mechanism for suites that cannot be redistributed,\n  with clear behavior when a suite is not locally available (the fallback path\n  identified by the licensing assessment).\n- Register the out-of-the-box suite catalog (suite names, lm-eval task names,\n  suite versions) so the execution path and the Dashboard can present the\n  selectable list.\n- Keep suite versions explicit in the catalog so persisted results remain\n  interpretable across suite version bumps (aligned with the canonical result\n  schema's version fields).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** a disconnected RHOAI installation, **when** a user selects a\n  redistributable standard suite (e.g. MMLU), **then** the evaluation runs\n  without any external dataset fetch, measured by a completed evaluation run in\n  a disconnected environment.\n- **Given** a suite classified as customer-fetch, **when** it is selected,\n  **then** the customer-fetch path is exercised with documented instructions\n  and defined failure behavior,