{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-83930076-8a17-4315-b8ef-4d587d86a387","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-892bdb1ea5dc0f02","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-j2d1wnw7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-E005.md","content":"# Evaluation result persistence and model version linking\n\n## Description\n\nImplement persistence of evaluation results in Model Registry, linked to the\nModel Registry version of the evaluated model, using the canonical result\nschema produced by the result-schema prototype. This makes Model Registry the\nsource of truth for \"which model version scored what\", enabling comparison and\npromotion decisions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the canonical result schema on ModelVersion custom properties per\n  the prototype's specification (per-benchmark scores, suite name and version,\n  cost/duration metadata, evaluated model version linkage).\n- Implement linking of an evaluation result to the registered model version of\n  the evaluated model, exposed through the Model Registry REST API\n  (model-registry.opendatahub.io).\n- Support retrieval of persisted results for a given model version, including\n  retrieval of two versions' results for side-by-side comparison (consumed by\n  the Dashboard and by pipeline-based promotion gating).\n- Validation of Model Registry as a passive consumer of the execution path:\n  the registry stores and links whatever results the execution path emits in\n  the canonical schema; no execution logic lives here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** an evaluation result in the canonical schema, **when** it is\n  persisted, **then** it is retrievable via the Model Registry REST API linked\n  to the correct ModelVersion, measured by a round-trip retrieval test.\n- **Given** two registered model versions with persisted evaluation results,\n  **when** both are retrieved, **then** their per-benchmark scores are\n  comparable field-by-field, measured by a comparison query.\n- **Given** results persisted under one benchmark-suite version, **when** the\n  suite version is bumped, **then** stored results remain interpretable\n  (per the prototype's version-bump test).\n- The schema committed here matches the prototype specification without\n  undocumented deviation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry\n  version of the evaluated model — full coverage.\n- HLR-8 (P2, cost/duration metadata): the schema and persistence path carry\n  these fields.\n\n## Dependencies (plain terms)\n\nBlocked by the canonical result schema prototype (the format this epic commits\nto Model Registry custom properties). If the prototype revises the schema, this\nepic's implementation is rewritten.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44210,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab59d602e88fa4e","agent_id":"ae71d3c6187365b78","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"a16163ea-3b57-4303-8f64-63abb682abff","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:55:27.560Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
