{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-83930076-8a17-4315-b8ef-4d587d86a387","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-92c3a0cbb3a7fdb7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-j2d1wnw7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-E006.md","content":"# Dashboard evaluation runs UI and model version comparison\n\n## Description\n\nIntegrate the evaluation capability into the Dashboard: users can see\nevaluation runs and their status, view per-benchmark scores, and compare two\nmodel versions side by side to inform promotion decisions. The Dashboard reads\nand writes Kubernetes CRs and component APIs; it owns no data plane.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add the evaluation section to the Dashboard (navigation, resource lists, and\n  run detail views) behind a feature flag via the OdhDashboardConfig CR,\n  reading the evaluation run resources and status exposed by the platform's\n  evaluation execution path.\n- Display per-benchmark scores for completed evaluation runs, sourced from\n  persisted evaluation results linked to model versions in Model Registry.\n- Implement the side-by-side comparison view of two model versions' evaluation\n  results (per-benchmark score alignment, suite version awareness).\n- Launch-entry integration: navigating from a served model or model version to\n  launching an evaluation against a selected benchmark suite, using the\n  execution surface selected by the execution-engine decision.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** evaluation runs in a data science project, **when** the user opens\n  the evaluation section, **then** runs and their status (running, succeeded,\n  failed) are listed, measured by UI verification against live run resources.\n- **Given** a completed evaluation run, **when** the user opens its detail\n  view, **then** per-benchmark scores are displayed from the persisted result,\n  measured by agreement with the Model Registry record.\n- **Given** two model versions with persisted evaluation results, **when** the\n  user opens the comparison view, **then** per-benchmark scores are shown side\n  by side, measured by a usability review with the documented comparison flow.\n- The integration follows the Dashboard's existing CR-driven integration\n  pattern and is feature-flagged via OdhDashboardConfig.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): Dashboard shows evaluation runs, status, per-benchmark scores,\n  and side-by-side comparison of two model versions — full coverage.\n\n## Dependencies (plain terms)\n\nDepends on the evaluation result persistence and model version linking\ncapability (builds against its retrieval API for scores and comparison), and is\ngated by the execution-engine decision (determines the run-resource surface the\nDashboard reads). If the engine decision selects a different execution surface,\nthis epic's data-source integration is rewritten.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44210,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab59d602e88fa4e","agent_id":"ae71d3c6187365b78","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"c9df1931-4bb5-4ff3-a100-9da45585490d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:55:37.544Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
