{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-83930076-8a17-4315-b8ef-4d587d86a387","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a08438b4031508d5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-j2d1wnw7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-E007.md","content":"# Evaluation step for Data Science Pipelines\n\n## Description\n\nEnable evaluations to be embedded as a step in a Data Science Pipeline so\npromotion flows can gate on scores (humans make the promotion decision — the\npipeline gates, it does not promote). Delivered as a reusable KFP v2 pipeline\ncomponent that launches an evaluation, waits for completion, and exposes the\nscores to downstream steps.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement a KFP v2 pipeline component (compatible with the Data Science\n  Pipelines Application / KFP v2 REST API and SDK) that launches an evaluation\n  of a served model against a selected benchmark suite using the execution\n  surface selected by the execution-engine decision.\n- Wait for evaluation completion and surface run status and per-benchmark\n  scores as component outputs so subsequent pipeline steps can gate on them.\n- Support reading persisted results linked to the evaluated model version from\n  Model Registry so a promotion flow can compare a candidate version's scores\n  against a threshold or a baseline version.\n- Document example promotion-gating usage (pipeline gate, human promotion) as\n  part of the component's usage material.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** a Data Science Pipeline, **when** the evaluation component is\n  included as a step, **then** the pipeline launches an evaluation of the\n  targeted served model and waits for its completion, measured by an end-to-end\n  example pipeline run.\n- **Given** a completed evaluation step, **when** downstream steps reference the\n  component outputs, **then** per-benchmark scores are available for gating\n  decisions, measured by a test pipeline that branches on a score threshold.\n- The component works against a DataSciencePipelinesApplication-managed\n  namespace using the KFP v2 API.\n- No automatic promotion is performed: the out-of-scope boundary (pipelines\n  gate, humans promote) is respected.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P1): evaluations embedded as a step in a Data Science Pipeline so\n  promotion flows can gate on scores — full coverage.\n\n## Dependencies (plain terms)\n\nDepends on the evaluation result persistence and model version linking\ncapability (reads persisted scores for gating), and is gated by the\nexecution-engine decision (determines the launch mechanism the component\nwraps). If the engine decision selects a different execution surface, this\nepic's launch integration is rewritten.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44210,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab59d602e88fa4e","agent_id":"ae71d3c6187365b78","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"1dc07231-2a8e-4117-91d9-3b7cb2d37ad7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:55:48.134Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
