e availability.\n7. Troubleshooting evaluation runs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** the delivered evaluation capability, **when** a user follows the\n  documentation from zero, **then** they can launch a standard-suite evaluation\n  and read its results, measured by documentation validation against the\n  implemented workflow.\n- The custom task authoring guide walks through defining and running one custom\n  task end to end.\n- All topics are technically reviewed against the implementation by the\n  component teams before publication.\n- Documentation covers the evaluation execution workflow as implemented —\n  including whichever execution approach was selected by the execution-engine\n  decision — verified during technical review.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-9 (P2): product documentation covers the evaluation workflow end to end,\n  including custom task authoring — full coverage.\n\n## Dependencies (plain terms)\n\nBlocked by all implementation work in the strategy (benchmark suite packaging,\nresult persistence, Dashboard integration, pipeline step, and the execution path\nas delivered), because the documentation describes the built system.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44210,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab59d602e88fa4e","agent_id":"ae71d3c6187365b78","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"4d0d9c1f-757a-42a6-9b74-8f80197c2113","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:55:58.385Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
