{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-33401141-ade3-4ee2-9f30-a01e5900a0f8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-92b9741800ffdca2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-j2d1wnw7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E009.md","content":"# Extend TrustyAI LMEvalJob as the single evaluation execution path\n\n## Description\n\nBranch A of the execution-engine decision: build on TrustyAI's LMEvalJob (the\nplatform's existing lm-evaluation-harness wrapper, currently Tech Preview) as\nthe single execution path for GenAI model evaluation. Users can launch an\nevaluation of a model served on the platform — a KServe endpoint or a Llama\nStack distribution — against a selected benchmark suite, including custom\nevaluation tasks, with results emitted in the canonical result schema.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the LMEvalJob capability so an evaluation can target a model served\n  on a KServe/ModelMesh inference endpoint or on a Llama Stack distribution\n  (LlamaStackDistribution), not just the job's current target surface.\n- Support user-defined custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and metrics)\n  running through the same job flow as standard lm-eval task names.\n- Emit evaluation results in the canonical result schema (per-benchmark\n  scores, suite name and version, evaluated model version linkage) and persist\n  them to Model Registry linked to the evaluated model version.\n- Record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) on evaluation\n  runs for capacity planning.\n- Job lifecycle and status reporting sufficient for the Dashboard's run list\n  and status views (running, succeeded, failed) and for pipeline-step\n  consumption.\n- Address Tech Preview maturity gaps identified by the execution-engine\n  decision for the capabilities this path now carries.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** a model served on a KServe endpoint and a selected standard\n  benchmark suite, **when** an evaluation is launched, **then** the job runs to\n  completion against that endpoint and records per-benchmark scores, measured\n  by a completed run with retrievable results.\n- **Given** a model served via a Llama Stack distribution, **when** an\n  evaluation is launched, **then** the same flow completes against the\n  distribution's endpoint, measured by a completed run.\n- **Given** a user-defined custom task (own dataset and metric), **when** it is\n  submitted through the evaluation flow, **then** it runs and scores like a\n  standard suite, measured by a custom-task run with persisted results.\n- **Given** a completed evaluation, **when** results are persisted, **then**\n  they follow the canonical result schema and are linked to the evaluated\n  model's Model Registry version, measured by retrieval from Model Registry.\n- Evaluation runs record tokens, wall-clock, and GPU time metadata.\n- Run status is observable throughout the job lifecycle.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected\n  benchmark suite — full coverage for branch A.\n- HLR-4 (P1): custom evaluation tasks through the same flow — full coverage.\n- HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration metadata recorded by evaluation runs — full\n  coverage.\n- HLR-3 (P0, writer side): this epic emits and persists the results that the\n  Model Registry persistence capability stores.\n\n## Dependencies (plain terms)\n\nExists only if the execution-engine decision selects extending LMEvalJob.\nDepends on that decision and on the canonical result schema prototype (the\njob code emits that schema). If the decision instead recommends a new\nevaluation service, this epic is dropped in favor of the new-service branch.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47533,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab59d602e88