ected standard\n  benchmark suite, **when** an evaluation is launched via the platform\n  evaluation API, **then** the service runs it to completion and records\n  per-benchmark scores, measured by a completed run with retrievable results.\n- **Given** a model served via a Llama Stack distribution, **when** an\n  evaluation is launched, **then** the same flow completes, measured by a\n  completed run.\n- **Given** a user-defined custom task (own dataset and metric), **when** it is\n  submitted through the evaluation flow, **then** it runs and scores like a\n  standard suite, measured by a custom-task run with persisted results.\n- **Given** a completed evaluation, **when** results are persisted, **then**\n  they follow the canonical result schema and are linked to the evaluated\n  model's Model Registry version, measured by retrieval from Model Registry.\n- Evaluation runs record tokens, wall-clock, and GPU time metadata.\n- Build pipeline green: the service builds through its Konflux pipeline\n  (onboarded in parallel) — first execution of this epic's code through the\n  pipeline must pass.\n- Dependencies match the validated license baseline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected\n  benchmark suite — full coverage for branch B.\n- HLR-4 (P1): custom evaluation tasks through the same flow — full coverage.\n- HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration metadata recorded by evaluation runs — full\n  coverage.\n- HLR-3 (P0, writer side): this epic emits and persists the results that the\n  Model Registry persistence capability stores.\n\n## Dependencies (plain terms)\n\nExists only if the execution-engine decision selects building a new evaluation\nservice. Depends on that decision, on the canonical result schema prototype\n(the service emits that schema), on the midstream repo onboarding (the code\nneeds its repository), and on license validation (dependency failures would\nchange the approach). Runs in parallel with Konflux 