{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfc2608ee30ba216","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: canonical evaluation result schema prototype'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: canonical evaluation result schema prototype\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's second open question: what is the canonical result\n30\tformat persisted to Model Registry custom properties, and does it survive\n31\tbenchmark-suite version bumps? The strategy requires prototyping against real\n32\tMMLU output before committing. The resulting schema is the shared contract\n33\tbetween the evaluation execution path (which writes results), Model Registry\n34\t(which persists and links them), and the Dashboard (which displays them).\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Run lm-evaluation-harness locally to capture representative real MMLU output\n39\t  (and at least one other standard suite, e.g. ARC or HellaSwag) including\n40\t  per-benchmark scores and run metadata.\n41\t- Design a canonical result schema expressible in Model Registry ModelVersion\n42\t  custom properties, covering: per-benchmark scores, benchmark-suite name and\n43\t  version, evaluated model version linkage, and cost/duration metadata (tokens,\n44\t  wall-clock, GPU time) needed for capacity planning.\n45\t- Prototype persistence of the schema through the Model Registry REST API\n46\t  (model-registry.opendatahub.io) onto ModelVersion custom properties and\n47\t  verify round-trip fidelity.\n48\t- Test schema behavior under benchmark-suite version bumps: does a stored\n49\t  result remain interpretable when the suite version changes, and does the\n50\t  schema support side-by-side comparison of two model versions?\n51\t- Deliver a written schema specification with the prototype results and a\n52\t  pass/fail verdict on version-bump survivability, including any schema\n53\t  revision needed.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- **Given** real lm-evaluation-harness MMLU output, **when** the prototype\n58\t  persists it to Model Registry custom properties via the REST API, **then**\n59\t  the stored result round-trips losslessly, measured by retrieving it and\n60\t  comparing against the source output.\n61\t- **Given** results stored under one benchmark-suite version, **when** the suite\n62\t  version is bumped, **then** previously stored results remain interpretable\n63\t  and comparable, measured by a documented version-bump test in the prototype\n64\t  report.\n65\t- The schema specification includes fields for cost/duration metadata (tokens,\n66\t  wall-clock, GPU time) and the evaluated model version linkage.\n67\t- The TrustyAI and Model Registry teams accept the schema as the contract the\n68\t  execution path will emit.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-3 (P0, results persisted and linked to Model Registry version): this\n73\t  investigation defines the format the persistence implementation commits to.\n74\t- HLR-8 (P2, cost/duration metadata): the schema must carry these fields.\n75\t- HLR-5 (P1, Dashboard comparison): the schema must support side-by-side\n76\t  comparison of two model versions.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bafeac65b5675e9e","agent_id":"a0d5c3e4fb04950c0","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"da1e7f82-68f7-47ef-bafe-2140a58dbe34","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:04:09.830Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfc2608ee30ba216","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
