{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d06346bde0155f4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: benchmark dataset licensing assessment'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: benchmark dataset licensing assessment\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's third open question: which standard benchmark suites can\n30\tbe redistributed by Red Hat in disconnected environments, and which must be\n31\tfetched by the customer? The answer determines the packaging approach for the\n32\tout-of-the-box benchmark suite delivery.\n33\t\n34\t## Scope\n35\t\n36\t- Enumerate the candidate standard suites exposed through lm-eval task names\n37\t  (at minimum MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag) together with their dataset licenses and\n38\t  any terms governing redistribution in a shipped product image or artifact.\n39\t- Classify each suite: redistributable (can be bundled) vs. customer-fetch\n40\t  (must be downloaded by the customer at installation/run time), with the\n41\t  license citation that justifies each classification.\n42\t- Identify any suites where the determination is uncertain and requires Red Hat\n43\t  legal review, and prepare the specific questions for that review.\n44\t- Deliver a written assessment that the benchmark packaging implementation can\n45\t  act on: the bundled list, the customer-fetch list, and the fallback behavior\n46\t  for non-redistributable suites.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- **Given** the candidate benchmark suites, **when** the licensing assessment\n51\t  is complete, **then** every suite is classified as redistributable or\n52\t  customer-fetch with a cited license basis.\n53\t- Suites with uncertain redistribution status are escalated to legal with\n54\t  specific questions, and the assessment records the escalation status.\n55\t- The packaging approach for out-of-the-box suites (bundle vs. fetch vs. mixed)\n56\t  is determinable directly from the assessment, measured by the packaging epic\n57\t  being able to proceed without re-analyzing licenses.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- HLR-2 (P0, standard suites available out of the box): this investigation\n62\t  determines how \"out of the box\" can be delivered per suite.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bafeac65b5675e9e","agent_id":"a0d5c3e4fb04950c0","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"905fa8f2-a3e5-4a25-bbc2-63ef0772455e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:04:10.930Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d06346bde0155f4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
