{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81afca82ceef797c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E006\n3\ttitle: Dashboard evaluation runs UI and model version comparison\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E005\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine decision selects a different execution\n16\t    surface than assumed, rewrite the Dashboard's run-resource data-source integration\n17\t    against the selected surface.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Dashboard evaluation runs UI and model version comparison\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tIntegrate the evaluation capability into the Dashboard: users can see\n40\tevaluation runs and their status, view per-benchmark scores, and compare two\n41\tmodel versions side by side to inform promotion decisions. The Dashboard reads\n42\tand writes Kubernetes CRs and component APIs; it owns no data plane.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Add the evaluation section to the Dashboard (navigation, resource lists, and\n47\t  run detail views) behind a feature flag via the OdhDashboardConfig CR,\n48\t  reading the evaluation run resources and status exposed by the platform's\n49\t  evaluation execution path.\n50\t- Display per-benchmark scores for completed evaluation runs, sourced from\n51\t  persisted evaluation results linked to model versions in Model Registry.\n52\t- Implement the side-by-side comparison view of two model versions' evaluation\n53\t  results (per-benchmark score alignment, suite version awareness).\n54\t- Launch-entry integration: navigating from a served model or model version to\n55\t  launching an evaluation against a selected benchmark suite, using the\n56\t  execution surface selected by the execution-engine decision.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- **Given** evaluation runs in a data science project, **when** the user opens\n61\t  the evaluation section, **then** runs and their status (running, succeeded,\n62\t  failed) are listed, measured by UI verification against live run resources.\n63\t- **Given** a completed evaluation run, **when** the user opens its detail\n64\t  view, **then** per-benchmark scores are displayed from the persisted result,\n65\t  measured by agreement with the Model Registry record.\n66\t- **Given** two model versions with persisted evaluation results, **when** the\n67\t  user opens the comparison view, **then** per-benchmark scores are shown side\n68\t  by side, measured by a usability review with the documented comparison flow.\n69\t- The integration follows the Dashboard's existing CR-driven integration\n70\t  pattern and is feature-flagged via OdhDashboardConfig.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-5 (P1): Dashboard shows evaluation runs, status, per-benchmark scores,\n75\t  and side-by-side comparison of two model versions — full coverage.\n76\t\n77\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n78\t\n79\tDepends on the evaluation result persistence and model version linking\n80\tcapability (builds against its retrieval API for scores and comparison), and is\n81\tgated by the execution-engine decision (determines the run-resource surface the\n82\tDashboard reads). If the engine decision selects a different execution surface,\n83\tthis epic's data-source integration is rewritten.\n84\t"}]},"parent_to