{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0c8be2dda318ea5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E010\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack eval provider backed by the TrustyAI execution path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E009\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not select extending\n17\t    LMEvalJob, this epic is dropped and the Llama Stack provider is wired to the new\n18\t    evaluation service instead.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack eval provider backed by the TrustyAI execution path\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch A of the execution-engine decision: implement Llama Stack's eval\n40\tprovider API as a provider backed by the platform's evaluation capability\n41\tdelivered through the extended TrustyAI LMEvalJob execution path, so agents and\n42\tapps built on Llama Stack get the same evaluation results as the platform flow.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Implement an eval provider for Llama Stack (provider-plugin model, configured\n47\t  per LlamaStackDistribution) that delegates evaluations to the TrustyAI\n48\t  execution path.\n49\t- Map the Llama Stack eval provider API operations onto the platform\n50\t  evaluation flow (launch evaluation against a served model, retrieve status\n51\t  and scores).\n52\t- Wire the provider as the production eval provider in the platform's Llama\n53\t  Stack distribution, replacing the current state where the eval provider API\n54\t  exists upstream but no production eval provider is wired in the platform\n55\t  distribution.\n56\t- Return results consistent with the canonical result schema so Llama\n57\t  Stack-based consumers see the same scores as the Dashboard and pipeline\n58\t  flows.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- **Given** a LlamaStackDistribution with the platform eval provider\n63\t  configured, **when** an agent or app calls the Llama Stack eval provider\n64\t  API, **then** an evaluation is launched through the platform execution path\n65\t  and results are returned, measured by an API-level test against a served\n66\t  model.\n67\t- **Given** the same model and suite evaluated via the platform flow and via\n68\t  the Llama Stack eval provider API, **then** the per-benchmark scores agree,\n69\t  measured by a comparison test.\n70\t- The provider is wired into the platform Llama Stack distribution\n71\t  configuration as the production eval provider.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-7 (P1): Llama Stack's eval provider API backed by the platform\n76\t  evaluation service — full coverage for branch A.\n77\t\n78\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n79\t\n80\tExists only if the execution-engine decision selects extending LMEvalJob.\n81\tDepends on that decision and on the extended TrustyAI LMEvalJob execution\n82\tcapability it builds against (framework before consumer). If the decision\n83\tinstead recommends a new evaluation service, this epic is dropped in favor of\n84\tthe new-service provider wiring.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bafeac65b5675e9e","agent_id":"a0d5c3e4fb04950c0","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"8fedbd28-42fb-40f7-972a-d507227a3039","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:04:26.853Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0c8b