{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e79db019275c902","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E012\n3\ttitle: Build the new evaluation service\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E009\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E010\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: remove\n18\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not select building\n19\t    a new evaluation service, this epic is dropped and the TrustyAI LMEvalJob extension\n20\t    epic is executed instead.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 0\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 0\n26\t  open_questions: 0\n27\t  external_dependency: 0\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 4\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Build the new evaluation service\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tBranch B of the execution-engine decision: implement the new evaluation\n42\tservice — the platform's single execution path for GenAI model evaluation. The\n43\tservice wraps lm-evaluation-harness, exposes the platform evaluation API, and\n44\tserves as the backend for Llama Stack's eval provider API. Users can launch an\n45\tevaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe endpoint or Llama Stack\n46\tdistribution) against a selected benchmark suite, including custom evaluation\n47\ttasks, with results persisted per the canonical result schema.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Implement the evaluation service: launching evaluations of models served on\n52\t  KServe endpoints and Llama Stack distributions against selected benchmark\n53\t  suites, executing them via lm-evaluation-harness, with job lifecycle and\n54\t  status reporting.\n55\t- Expose the platform evaluation API consumed by the Dashboard, Data Science\n56\t  Pipelines, and the Llama Stack eval provider wiring.\n57\t- Support user-defined custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and metrics)\n58\t  through the same flow as standard lm-eval task names.\n59\t- Emit results in the canonical result schema and persist them to Model\n60\t  Registry linked to the evaluated model version.\n61\t- Record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) on evaluation\n62\t  runs for capacity planning.\n63\t- Deployment story for the service within the platform (how it is installed\n64\t  and managed per data science project), per the execution-engine decision's\n65\t  placement recommendation.\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- **Given** a model served on a KServe endpoint and a selected standard\n70\t  benchmark suite, **when** an evaluation is launched via the platform\n71\t  evaluation API, **then** the service runs it to completion and records\n72\t  per-benchmark scores, measured by a completed run with retrievable results.\n73\t- **Given** a model served via a Llama Stack distribution, **when** an\n74\t  evaluation is launched, **then** the same flow completes, measured by a\n75\t  completed run.\n76\t- **Given** a user-defined custom task (own dataset and metric), **when** it is\n77\t  submitted through the evaluation flow, **then** it runs and scores like a\n78\t  standard suite, measured by a custom-task run with persisted results.\n79\t- **Given** a completed evaluation, **when** results are persisted, **then**\n80\t  they follow the canonical result schema and are linked to the evaluated\n81\t  model's Model Registry version, measured by retrieval from Model Registry.\n82\t- Evaluation runs record tokens, wall-clock, and GPU time metadata.\n83\t- Build pipeline green: the service builds through its Konflux pipeline\n84\t  (onboarded in parallel) — first execution of this epic's code through the\n85\t  pipeline must pass.\n86\t- Dependencies match the validated license baseline.\n87\t\n88\t## HLR Traceability\n89\t\n90\t- HLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected\n91\t  benchmark suite — full coverage for branch B.\n92\t- HLR-4 (P1): custom evaluation tasks through the same flow — full coverage.\n93\t- HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration metadata recorded by evaluation runs — full\n94\t  coverage.\n95\t- HLR-3 (P0, writer side): this epic emits and persists the results that the\n96\t  Model Registry persistence capability stores.\n97\t\n98\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n99\t\n100\tExists only if the execution-engine decision selects building a new evaluation\n101\tservice. Depends on that decision, on the canonical result schema prototype\n102\t(the service emits that schema), on the midstream repo onboarding (the code\n103\tneeds its repository), and on license validation (dependency failures would\n104\tchange the approach). Runs in parallel with Konflux onboarding — the coupling\n105\tis enforced by the build-pipeline-green acceptance criterion, not by a\n106\tdependency. If the decision instead extends TrustyAI's LMEvalJob, this epic is\n107\tdropped in favor of the LMEvalJob extension.\n108\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bafeac65b5675e9e","agent_id":"a0d5c3e4fb04950c0","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"475e0028-1076-4b72-ae38-f26493d8f870","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:04:34.570Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e79db019275c902","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
