{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3228d4c5c36cb05","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E013\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack eval provider backed by the new evaluation service\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E012\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine investigation does not select building\n17\t    a new evaluation service, this epic is dropped and the Llama Stack provider is\n18\t    instead backed by the TrustyAI LMEvalJob execution path.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack eval provider backed by the new evaluation service\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch B of the execution-engine decision: wire Llama Stack's eval provider\n40\tAPI to the new platform evaluation service, so agents and apps built on Llama\n41\tStack get the same evaluation results as the platform flow. The new service\n42\tnatively serves the provider backend; this epic wires it into the platform's\n43\tLlama Stack distribution.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Wire the Llama Stack eval provider in the platform's Llama Stack\n48\t  distribution (LlamaStackDistribution, provider plugins configured per\n49\t  distribution) to point at the new evaluation service as its backend.\n50\t- Map the Llama Stack eval provider API operations onto the service's platform\n51\t  evaluation API (launch evaluation against a served model, retrieve status\n52\t  and scores).\n53\t- Replace the current state where the eval provider API exists upstream but no\n54\t  production eval provider is wired in the platform distribution.\n55\t- Return results consistent with the canonical result schema so Llama\n56\t  Stack-based consumers see the same scores as the Dashboard and pipeline\n57\t  flows.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- **Given** a LlamaStackDistribution with the platform eval provider\n62\t  configured, **when** an agent or app calls the Llama Stack eval provider\n63\t  API, **then** an evaluation is launched through the new evaluation service\n64\t  and results are returned, measured by an API-level test against a served\n65\t  model.\n66\t- **Given** the same model and suite evaluated via the platform flow and via\n67\t  the Llama Stack eval provider API, **then** the per-benchmark scores agree,\n68\t  measured by a comparison test.\n69\t- The provider is wired into the platform Llama Stack distribution\n70\t  configuration as the production eval provider.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-7 (P1): Llama Stack's eval provider API backed by the platform\n75\t  evaluation service — full coverage for branch B.\n76\t\n77\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n78\t\n79\tExists only if the execution-engine decision selects building a new evaluation\n80\tservice. Depends on that decision and on the new evaluation service it builds\n81\tagainst (framework before consumer). If the decision instead extends\n82\tTrustyAI's LMEvalJob, this epic is dropped in favor of the TrustyAI-backed\n83\tprovider adapter.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bafeac65b5675e9e","agent_id":"a0d5c3e4fb04950c0","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"6b2299b5-2d74-4cee-9b67-5ff0ccbc5662","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:04:35.780Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3228d4c5c36cb05","permiss