{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89adddb9aacd8b50","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E005\n3\ttitle: Evaluation result persistence and model version linking\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the schema prototype revises the canonical format (e.g. to\n15\t    survive benchmark-suite version bumps), rewrite the persistence implementation\n16\t    to the revised schema before release.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Evaluation result persistence and model version linking\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplement persistence of evaluation results in Model Registry, linked to the\n39\tModel Registry version of the evaluated model, using the canonical result\n40\tschema produced by the result-schema prototype. This makes Model Registry the\n41\tsource of truth for \"which model version scored what\", enabling comparison and\n42\tpromotion decisions.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Implement the canonical result schema on ModelVersion custom properties per\n47\t  the prototype's specification (per-benchmark scores, suite name and version,\n48\t  cost/duration metadata, evaluated model version linkage).\n49\t- Implement linking of an evaluation result to the registered model version of\n50\t  the evaluated model, exposed through the Model Registry REST API\n51\t  (model-registry.opendatahub.io).\n52\t- Support retrieval of persisted results for a given model version, including\n53\t  retrieval of two versions' results for side-by-side comparison (consumed by\n54\t  the Dashboard and by pipeline-based promotion gating).\n55\t- Validation of Model Registry as a passive consumer of the execution path:\n56\t  the registry stores and links whatever results the execution path emits in\n57\t  the canonical schema; no execution logic lives here.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- **Given** an evaluation result in the canonical schema, **when** it is\n62\t  persisted, **then** it is retrievable via the Model Registry REST API linked\n63\t  to the correct ModelVersion, measured by a round-trip retrieval test.\n64\t- **Given** two registered model versions with persisted evaluation results,\n65\t  **when** both are retrieved, **then** their per-benchmark scores are\n66\t  comparable field-by-field, measured by a comparison query.\n67\t- **Given** results persisted under one benchmark-suite version, **when** the\n68\t  suite version is bumped, **then** stored results remain interpretable\n69\t  (per the prototype's version-bump test).\n70\t- The schema committed here matches the prototype specification without\n71\t  undocumented deviation.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry\n76\t  version of the evaluated model — full coverage.\n77\t- HLR-8 (P2, cost/duration metadata): the schema and persistence path carry\n78\t  these fields.\n79\t\n80\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n81\t\n82\tBlocked by the canonical result schema prototype (the format this epic commits\n83\tto Model Registry custom properties). If the prototype revises the schema, this\n84\tepic's implementation is rewritten.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5c9c8c774e19669","agent_id":"aa44b0c53f6d9eafc","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-b