{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f93f36b7ecf9ccf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E007\n3\ttitle: Evaluation step for Data Science Pipelines\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Data Science Pipelines\n6\tteam: RHOAI Pipelines\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E005\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the execution-engine decision selects a different execution\n16\t    surface than assumed, rewrite the pipeline component's launch/wait integration\n17\t    against the selected surface.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Evaluation step for Data Science Pipelines\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tEnable evaluations to be embedded as a step in a Data Science Pipeline so\n40\tpromotion flows can gate on scores (humans make the promotion decision — the\n41\tpipeline gates, it does not promote). Delivered as a reusable KFP v2 pipeline\n42\tcomponent that launches an evaluation, waits for completion, and exposes the\n43\tscores to downstream steps.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Implement a KFP v2 pipeline component (compatible with the Data Science\n48\t  Pipelines Application / KFP v2 REST API and SDK) that launches an evaluation\n49\t  of a served model against a selected benchmark suite using the execution\n50\t  surface selected by the execution-engine decision.\n51\t- Wait for evaluation completion and surface run status and per-benchmark\n52\t  scores as component outputs so subsequent pipeline steps can gate on them.\n53\t- Support reading persisted results linked to the evaluated model version from\n54\t  Model Registry so a promotion flow can compare a candidate version's scores\n55\t  against a threshold or a baseline version.\n56\t- Document example promotion-gating usage (pipeline gate, human promotion) as\n57\t  part of the component's usage material.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- **Given** a Data Science Pipeline, **when** the evaluation component is\n62\t  included as a step, **then** the pipeline launches an evaluation of the\n63\t  targeted served model and waits for its completion, measured by an end-to-end\n64\t  example pipeline run.\n65\t- **Given** a completed evaluation step, **when** downstream steps reference the\n66\t  component outputs, **then** per-benchmark scores are available for gating\n67\t  decisions, measured by a test pipeline that branches on a score threshold.\n68\t- The component works against a DataSciencePipelinesApplication-managed\n69\t  namespace using the KFP v2 API.\n70\t- No automatic promotion is performed: the out-of-scope boundary (pipelines\n71\t  gate, humans promote) is respected.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-6 (P1): evaluations embedded as a step in a Data Science Pipeline so\n76\t  promotion flows can gate on scores — full coverage.\n77\t\n78\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n79\t\n80\tDepends on the evaluation result persistence and model version linking\n81\tcapability (reads persisted scores for gating), and is gated by the\n82\texecution-engine decision (determines the launch mechanism the component\n83\twraps). If the engine decision selects a different execution surface, this\n84\tepic's launch integration is rewritten.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5c9c8c774e19669","agent_id":"aa44b0c53f6d9eafc","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"7964f28c-c0f0