{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b481c79fc41ecb0e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: evaluation execution engine decision'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: evaluation execution engine decision\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's first open question: should the platform build on\n30\tTrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview, already wrapping lm-evaluation-harness) as\n31\tthe single evaluation execution path, or is a new evaluation service needed that\n32\tcan also serve Llama Stack's eval provider API? This is the gating decision for\n33\tthe entire execution layer of the evaluation capability — it determines which\n34\tdownstream implementation epics exist and what they do.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Analyze the LMEvalJob CRD and job runner (trustyai-service-operator, upstream\n39\t  and midstream) against the full set of execution requirements: evaluating\n40\t  models served on KServe endpoints and on Llama Stack distributions, custom\n41\t  evaluation tasks (user-supplied datasets and metrics), and result emission.\n42\t- Analyze Llama Stack's eval provider API surface (meta-llama/llama-stack\n43\t  upstream) and determine what a platform-backed provider must implement, and\n44\t  whether the LMEvalJob path can back it (e.g. via an adapter) or whether the\n45\t  API shape demands a purpose-built service.\n46\t- Assess operational fit: multi-tenancy per data science project, job lifecycle\n47\t  and status reporting, resource/GPU scheduling behavior, and Tech Preview\n48\t  maturity risks of building the P0 path on LMEvalJob.\n49\t- Produce a written recommendation with a decision record covering both\n50\t  outcomes, including repo/component placement if a new service is recommended\n51\t  (new opendatahub-io repo vs. extension of an existing one), and the concrete\n52\t  API/CR surface each downstream epic would build against.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- **Given** the LMEvalJob source and the Llama Stack eval provider API\n57\t  specification, **when** the gap analysis is complete, **then** a\n58\t  recommendation document exists that selects exactly one execution approach,\n59\t  with an explicit rationale and a list of gaps each approach must close.\n60\t- **Given** the recommendation, **then** the downstream execution-path plan for\n61\t  the selected outcome is confirmed as buildable (or adjusted), measured by\n62\t  sign-off from the TrustyAI team and the RHOAI GenAI team.\n63\t- The decision record states the API/CR surface downstream consumers\n64\t  (Dashboard, Data Science Pipelines, Llama Stack provider) will build against\n65\t  for the selected outcome.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0, launch evaluation of served model): this investigation decides the\n70\t  architecture of the epic that delivers HLR-1.\n71\t- HLR-7 (P1, Llama Stack eval provider backed by platform service): the\n72\t  provider-API analysis here determines whether HLR-7 is an adapter or native\n73\t  wiring.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bee1af9f44323e62","agent_id":"ac6fccb22a2a1fcbe","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"20bb92c4-ef2d-4a40-b740-1eeba2e920a5","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:20:36.192Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b481c79fc41ecb0e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source