{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85730780ad3fda5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E004\n3\ttitle: Standard benchmark suites available out of the box\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: 'If the licensing assessment reclassifies suites, rework the\n15\t    packaging approach: bundles become customer-fetch mechanisms (or vice versa) per\n16\t    the final classification.'\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Standard benchmark suites available out of the box\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tDeliver the platform's out-of-the-box library of standard benchmark suites\n39\t(e.g. MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag exposed through lm-eval task names) so users can\n40\tselect a standard suite when launching an evaluation, per the licensing\n41\tassessment's packaging determination. This epic packages and ships the suites;\n42\tit does not change the execution engine itself.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Package the standard benchmark suites determined to be redistributable so\n47\t  they are available in disconnected environments without customer action.\n48\t- Provide the customer-fetch mechanism for suites that cannot be redistributed,\n49\t  with clear behavior when a suite is not locally available (the fallback path\n50\t  identified by the licensing assessment).\n51\t- Register the out-of-the-box suite catalog (suite names, lm-eval task names,\n52\t  suite versions) so the execution path and the Dashboard can present the\n53\t  selectable list.\n54\t- Keep suite versions explicit in the catalog so persisted results remain\n55\t  interpretable across suite version bumps (aligned with the canonical result\n56\t  schema's version fields).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- **Given** a disconnected RHOAI installation, **when** a user selects a\n61\t  redistributable standard suite (e.g. MMLU), **then** the evaluation runs\n62\t  without any external dataset fetch, measured by a completed evaluation run in\n63\t  a disconnected environment.\n64\t- **Given** a suite classified as customer-fetch, **when** it is selected,\n65\t  **then** the customer-fetch path is exercised with documented instructions\n66\t  and defined failure behavior, measured by a successful customer-fetched run.\n67\t- The out-of-the-box catalog lists suite name, lm-eval task name, and suite\n68\t  version for every packaged suite.\n69\t- Packaging decisions trace line-by-line to the licensing assessment\n70\t  (redistributable → bundled; customer-fetch → fetch mechanism).\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box — full\n75\t  coverage.\n76\t\n77\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n78\t\n79\tBlocked by the benchmark dataset licensing assessment (which suites may be\n80\tbundled vs. must be customer-fetched). If the assessment reclassifies suites,\n81\tthis epic's packaging approach is rewritten.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bee1af9f44323e62","agent_id":"ac6fccb22a2a1fcbe","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-be21-820bec1a5f5b","uuid":"8c830864-07d9-4e7d-814f-094bf32c388c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:20:40.118Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85730780ad3fda5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type"