 the Model Registry REST API\n51\t  (model-registry.opendatahub.io).\n52\t- Support retrieval of persisted results for a given model version, including\n53\t  retrieval of two versions' results for side-by-side comparison (consumed by\n54\t  the Dashboard and by pipeline-based promotion gating).\n55\t- Validation of Model Registry as a passive consumer of the execution path:\n56\t  the registry stores and links whatever results the execution path emits in\n57\t  the canonical schema; no execution logic lives here.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- **Given** an evaluation result in the canonical schema, **when** it is\n62\t  persisted, **then** it is retrievable via the Model Registry REST API linked\n63\t  to the correct ModelVersion, measured by a round-trip retrieval test.\n64\t- **Given** two registered model versions with persisted evaluation results,\n65\t  **when** both are retrieved, **then** their per-benchmark scores are\n66\t  comparable field-by-field, measured by a comparison query.\n67\t- **Given** results persisted under one benchmark-suite version, **when** the\n68\t  suite version is bumped, **then** stored results remain interpretable\n69\t  (per the prototype's version-bump test).\n70\t- The schema committed here matches the prototype specification without\n71\t  undocumented deviation.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results persisted and linked to the Model Registry\n76\t  version of the evaluated model — full coverage.\n77\t- HLR-8 (P2, cost/duration metadata): the schema and persistence path carry\n78\t  these fields.\n79\t\n80\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n81\t\n82\tBlocked by the canonical result schema prototype (the format this epic commits\n83\tto Model Registry custom properties). If the prototype revises the schema, this\n84\tepic's implementation is rewritten.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bee1af9f44323e62","agent_id":"ac6fccb22a2a1fcbe","session_id":"b48ac94b-45e8-413d-b